orm","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":9,"section_title":"The permanent lower bound and its consequences","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:552b0e981a6e0dd4f59d7593ce3c4c2d0b56f00a429559122f851ddb6461e56d","file":"preprints/A-cubic-lower-bound-for-border-determinantal-complexity-of-the-permanent-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/consequences.tex","line":107,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a06430e78df2a8a3f00ebe53cf04620cd9e7d664bbd11143ca8ed1b2feacc2d2","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-cubic-lower-bound-for-border-determinantal-complexity-of-the-permanent-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/consequences.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:552b0e981a6e0dd4f59d7593ce3c4c2d0b56f00a429559122f851ddb6461e56d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-cubic-lower-bound-for-border-determinantal-complexity-of-the-permanent-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/consequences.tex#L107"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:smooth-initial-form}\nLet $g\\in\\C[x_1,\\ldots,x_d]$, where $d\\ge2$, and let $a\\in\\C^d$.\nSuppose that the lowest nonzero homogeneous term $G_r(x)$ of $g(a+x)$\nhas degree $r\\ge2$ and defines a smooth hypersurface in $\\PP^{d-1}$.\nThen\n\\[\n \\bdc(g)\\ge\\frac{(r-1)(d-1)}{4e}.\n\\]\nThe same lower bound holds for $\\dc(g)$."}
